WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.656
c. 200 BC · Llandough hill, above the
River Ely

2
00:00:02.696 --> 00:00:05.880
Spoken in Welsh, the living descendant of
the Brittonic they spoke

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.713
[in Welsh] Will the weather hold today?
Smoke's going straight up.

4
00:00:11.753 --> 00:00:14.848
No wind, no rain. We'll get the corn in.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.763
[in Welsh] Heads only, mind. Cut them
high.

6
00:00:18.803 --> 00:00:21.835
Leave the straw standing for the cattle.

7
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:39.095
[in Welsh] The boy's bringing the cattle
up off the marsh, before the big tides
come.

8
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.211
[in Welsh] Good. They're better up here on
the hill.

9
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.459
[in Welsh] Not this year.

10
00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:51.298
The pig's fat, the store's full, and the
cloth's nearly done for the little one's
cloak.

11
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:05.140
[in Welsh] Listen, little one. Geese,
going over. The cold's coming.

12
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.770
Bring wood in by the door tonight.

